# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Solr (with the vulnerable Log4j 2.14.1) in the
# background and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "patched the jars but never restarted Solr" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Solr cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART Solr after replacing the Log4j
# jars, not merely start it if absent - the service is already up with the
# vulnerable classes loaded into the running JVM.
